    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d216">

                <pb facs="0206" n="200" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg200"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr.
                            Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-05-14"><hi rendition="#italic">May 14,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith for your information
                    copy of an agreement<anchor n="*" xml:id="d216-f1"/> between the Government of
                    the United States and the Imperial Government of Russia for a modus vivendi in
                    relation to the fur-seal fisheries in Bering Sea and the North Pacific Ocean,
                    concluded on May 4, 1894.</p>
                <p>I also inclose translation of a note of the 4th instant<anchor n="†"
                        xml:id="d216-f2"/> from the Russian minister in this capital, wherein he
                    declares that the Imperial Government is prepared to negotiate and sign with the
                    United States, England, Mid Japan a treaty, in virtue of which the principles
                    and regulations of the Paris Tribunal of Arbitration shall be applicable,
                    indifferently, to all the waters of the Pacific Ocean situated north of the.
                    thirty-fifth parallel of north latitude.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. F. Uhl</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Acting Secretary</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
